{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "d5c4a616-11a4-4a9e-a3b3-7d8f6c16f001",
    "name": "RTech Backend API",
    "description": "Postman collection for the RTech Backend Code Challenge.\n\nPrerequisites:\n1. Start the API using `dotnet run --launch-profile http` from RTech.Api.\n2. Confirm SQL Server is running and the DDL + seed scripts have been executed.\n3. Use `baseUrl` matching the actual listening URL (default http://localhost:5204).\n\nRun order:\n- Run folders 00 through 04 in order.\n- Folder 01 creates a unique user and ship and stores their IDs.\n- Folder 02 uses those generated IDs.\n- Crew and financial tests use seeded SHIP01 and SHIP02.\n\nNote: The create requests write test records to your database. A new uniquely named\nuser and ship are created each time you run the collection. The other requests are read-only.\nThe duplicate-create, invalid-input, and inactive/unknown ship requests are negative tests\nwhose expected non-2xx status codes are asserted as passing tests.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "00 - Reference Data",
      "description": "Run first. Confirms the seeded ships and users are visible.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List active ships",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ships?includeInactive=false",
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "includeInactive",
                  "value": "false",
                  "disabled": false
                }
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "ships"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected to include SHIP01, SHIP02, SHIP03 and SHIP05; SHIP04 is inactive."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"HTTP 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const rows = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"Response is an array\", () => pm.expect(rows).to.be.an(\"array\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"SHIP01 exists\", () => pm.expect(rows.some(x => x.shipCode === \"SHIP01\")).to.be.true);",
                  "pm.test(\"Inactive SHIP04 is excluded\", () => pm.expect(rows.some(x => x.shipCode === \"SHIP04\")).to.be.false);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "List all ships (including inactive)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ships?includeInactive=true",
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "includeInactive",
                  "value": "true",
                  "disabled": false
                }
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "ships"
              ]
            },
            "description": ""
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"HTTP 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const rows = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"SHIP04 is included when requested\", () => pm.expect(rows.some(x => x.shipCode === \"SHIP04\")).to.be.true);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "List active users",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users?includeInactive=false",
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "includeInactive",
                  "value": "false",
                  "disabled": false
                }
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "users"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected to include seeded accounts such as admin and ops.manager."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"HTTP 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const rows = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"Response is an array\", () => pm.expect(rows).to.be.an(\"array\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"Seeded admin user exists\", () => pm.expect(rows.some(x => x.username === \"admin\")).to.be.true);"
